# doq: fixed after review 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setup {#setup}"
msgstr "Penyiapan {#setup}"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This section imports the tools and defines the shell-model helpers the workflow needs, in the order\n"
"the workflow uses them. The physics behind each one is derived in the [Appendix](#appendix); the\n"
"comments describe each function's role in the workflow.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bagian ini mengimpor tools dan mendefinisikan helper model-shell yang dibutuhkan workflow, dalam urutan\n"
"workflow menggunakannya. Fisika di balik masing-masing diturunkan di [Appendix](#appendix); komentarnya\n"
"menjelaskan peran masing-masing fungsi dalam workflow.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Two interaction files are unpacked first. Both are published parameter sets, embedded here so the\n"
"notebook is self-contained: `usda.snt` is the USDA $sd$-shell Hamiltonian [\\[2\\]](#references) and\n"
"`gxpf1.snt` is the GXPF1 $pf$-shell Hamiltonian [\\[3\\]](#references).\n"
msgstr ""
"Dua file interaksi dibongkar terlebih dahulu. Keduanya adalah kumpulan parameter yang sudah dipublikasikan, disematkan di sini agar\n"
"notebook menjadi self-contained: `usda.snt` adalah Hamiltonian shell-$sd$ USDA [\\[2\\]](#references) dan\n"
"`gxpf1.snt` adalah Hamiltonian shell-$pf$ GXPF1 [\\[3\\]](#references).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The model space and the qubit register {#the-model-space-and-the-qubit-register}"
msgstr "Ruang model dan register qubit {#the-model-space-and-the-qubit-register}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"An `.snt` file holds the model space, the single-particle energies, and the $J$-coupled two-body\n"
"matrix elements. For the mass-dependent interactions used here, the third and fourth fields of the two-body\n"
"header specify the reference mass\n"
"$A_{\\mathrm{ref}}$ at which the interaction was fitted and the exponent of its mass dependence. Both\n"
"files carry the exponent $-0.3$, with $A_{\\mathrm{ref}} = 18$ for USDA and $42$ for GXPF1, so the\n"
"tabulated matrix elements must be rescaled by $(A/A_{\\mathrm{ref}})^{-0.3}$ for the nucleus being\n"
"computed [\\[2\\]](#references), [\\[3\\]](#references). Single-particle energies are not rescaled. Skipping\n"
"this step changes the correlation energy by a few percent.\n"
msgstr ""
"File `.snt` menyimpan ruang model, energi single-particle, dan elemen matriks two-body\n"
"yang $J$-coupled. Untuk interaksi yang bergantung massa yang digunakan di sini, field ketiga dan keempat dari header\n"
"two-body menentukan massa referensi\n"
"$A_{\\mathrm{ref}}$ saat interaksi tersebut dicocokkan dan eksponen dari ketergantungan massanya. Kedua\n"
"file membawa eksponen $-0.3$, dengan $A_{\\mathrm{ref}} = 18$ untuk USDA dan $42$ untuk GXPF1, sehingga\n"
"elemen matriks yang ditabulasikan harus diskalakan ulang dengan $(A/A_{\\mathrm{ref}})^{-0.3}$ untuk nukleus yang\n"
"sedang dihitung [\\[2\\]](#references), [\\[3\\]](#references). Energi single-particle tidak diskalakan ulang. Melewati\n"
"langkah ini mengubah energi korelasi sebesar beberapa persen.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The energies that follow are *valence* energies, measured from the inert core; they are not experimental\n"
"separation energies.\n"
msgstr ""
"Energi-energi berikut adalah energi *valence*, diukur dari core yang inert; energi tersebut bukan energi\n"
"separasi eksperimental.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Clebsch-Gordan recoupling {#clebsch-gordan-recoupling}"
msgstr "Recoupling Clebsch-Gordan {#clebsch-gordan-recoupling}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Equation (2) requires Clebsch-Gordan coefficients for half-integer angular momenta. Every argument is\n"
"passed as *twice* its physical value, so $j = 5/2$ enters as `5` and the arithmetic stays exact.\n"
msgstr ""
"Persamaan (2) membutuhkan koefisien Clebsch-Gordan untuk angular momentum setengah-integer. Setiap argumen\n"
"dilewatkan sebagai *dua kali* nilai fisiknya, sehingga $j = 5/2$ dimasukkan sebagai `5` dan aritmatikanya tetap eksak.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`Interaction.v_ms` handles lookups of the interaction matrix elements. An `.snt` file stores each\n"
"matrix element once, so a lookup might need the antisymmetrized pair-exchange phase $-(-1)^{j_a + j_b - J}$ on either\n"
"side, and the bra and ket might be stored in either order.\n"
msgstr ""
"`Interaction.v_ms` menangani lookup elemen matriks interaksi. File `.snt` menyimpan setiap\n"
"elemen matriks sekali, sehingga sebuah lookup mungkin membutuhkan fase pertukaran-pasangan antisimetrik $-(-1)^{j_a + j_b - J}$ di salah satu\n"
"sisi, dan bra maupun ket mungkin disimpan dalam urutan apa pun.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Matrix elements and the symmetry test {#matrix-elements-and-the-symmetry-test}"
msgstr "Elemen matriks dan tes simetri {#matrix-elements-and-the-symmetry-test}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A determinant is a sorted tuple of occupied qubit indices. Two determinants differing in more than\n"
"two occupied states have a vanishing matrix element; otherwise, the Slater-Condon rules give a short\n"
"sum over the interaction, multiplied by a fermionic sign counting how many occupied states lie between the\n"
"operators in the fixed register ordering.\n"
msgstr ""
"Determinant adalah tuple terurut dari indeks qubit yang terisi. Dua determinant yang berbeda pada lebih dari\n"
"dua state yang terisi memiliki elemen matriks nol; jika tidak, aturan Slater-Condon memberikan penjumlahan singkat\n"
"atas interaksi, dikalikan dengan tanda fermionic yang menghitung berapa banyak state terisi yang terletak di antara\n"
"operator dalam urutan register yang tetap.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-09-29 · verified 2026-09-30
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`symmetry_allowed` is the integer test that all four exact quantum numbers reduce to. It is used both\n"
"to filter samples and to enumerate the exact basis for the runs small enough to check.\n"
msgstr ""
"`symmetry_allowed` adalah tes integer yang menjadi bentuk akhir dari keempat pemeriksaan bilangan kuantum eksak tersebut. Tes ini digunakan baik\n"
"untuk menyaring sampel maupun untuk mengenumerasi basis eksak bagi run yang cukup kecil untuk diperiksa.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The reference determinant {#the-reference-determinant}"
msgstr "Determinant referensi {#the-reference-determinant}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The ansatz is built on top of a single determinant, so that determinant should be the best one\n"
"available. Filling the lowest single-particle energies ignores the two-body interaction. In these model\n"
"spaces, that choice gives an energy 1–2 MeV above the lowest-energy determinant.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ansatz dibangun di atas satu determinant, sehingga determinant tersebut harus menjadi yang terbaik yang\n"
"tersedia. Mengisi energi single-particle terendah mengabaikan interaksi two-body. Dalam ruang model\n"
"ini, pilihan tersebut memberikan energi 1–2 MeV di atas determinant dengan energi terendah.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Restricting to fillings made of time-reversed $(+m_j, -m_j)$ pairs forces $M_J = 0$ exactly and\n"
"leaves only $\\binom{n_{\\mathrm{pairs}}}{k}$ candidates per species (a few thousand at most), so the\n"
"best one can be found by searching them all on the full diagonal $\\langle \\Phi | H | \\Phi \\rangle$.\n"
"Ties go to the most strongly aligned pairs, where the $J = 0$ pairing force is strongest. In every\n"
"case in this tutorial that can be checked against a full enumeration, the search returns the global\n"
"lowest-diagonal determinant, which is also the largest single component of the exact ground state.\n"
msgstr ""
"Membatasi ke pengisian yang terdiri dari pasangan time-reversed $(+m_j, -m_j)$ memaksa $M_J = 0$ secara eksak dan\n"
"hanya menyisakan $\\binom{n_{\\mathrm{pairs}}}{k}$ kandidat per spesies (paling banyak beberapa ribu), sehingga\n"
"yang terbaik bisa ditemukan dengan mencari semuanya pada diagonal penuh $\\langle \\Phi | H | \\Phi \\rangle$.\n"
"Seri diselesaikan dengan pasangan yang paling kuat selaras, di mana gaya pairing $J = 0$ paling kuat. Pada setiap\n"
"kasus dalam tutorial ini yang bisa diperiksa terhadap enumerasi penuh, pencarian mengembalikan determinant\n"
"dengan diagonal terendah secara global, yang juga merupakan komponen tunggal terbesar dari ground state eksak.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The excitation pool and its perturbative ranking {#the-excitation-pool-and-its-perturbative-ranking}"
msgstr "Pool eksitasi dan perankingan perturbatifnya {#the-excitation-pool-and-its-perturbative-ranking}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Correlation is carried by two-particle–two-hole ($2p2h$) excitations from the reference. Two\n"
"selection rules reduce the pool before any circuit is built: an excitation must conserve $M_J$, and the hole pair and particle\n"
"pair must be able to couple to a common total $J$, which is a triangle inequality.\n"
msgstr ""
"Korelasi dibawa oleh eksitasi two-particle–two-hole ($2p2h$) dari referensi. Dua\n"
"aturan seleksi mengurangi pool sebelum circuit apa pun dibangun: eksitasi harus mengonservasi $M_J$, dan pasangan hole dan pasangan\n"
"particle harus bisa coupling ke total $J$ yang sama, yang merupakan pertidaksamaan segitiga.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The remaining excitations are ranked by the Epstein-Nesbet second-order score of selected configuration interaction\n"
"[\\[4\\]](#references),\n"
msgstr ""
"Eksitasi yang tersisa diranking berdasarkan skor orde kedua Epstein-Nesbet dari selected configuration interaction\n"
"[\\[4\\]](#references),\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation}\n"
"\\tag{3}\n"
"s_\\alpha = \\frac{|\\langle \\Phi_{\\mathrm{ref}} | H | \\alpha \\rangle|^2}{|\\Delta_\\alpha|},\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\Delta_\\alpha = H_{\\mathrm{ref},\\mathrm{ref}} - H_{\\alpha\\alpha},\n"
"\\end{equation}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation}\n"
"\\tag{3}\n"
"s_\\alpha = \\frac{|\\langle \\Phi_{\\mathrm{ref}} | H | \\alpha \\rangle|^2}{|\\Delta_\\alpha|},\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\Delta_\\alpha = H_{\\mathrm{ref},\\mathrm{ref}} - H_{\\alpha\\alpha},\n"
"\\end{equation}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"which estimates how much correlation energy each excitation carries. The same two numbers fix the\n"
"circuit angle: with $V = \\langle \\Phi_{\\mathrm{ref}} | H | \\alpha \\rangle$, the first-order amplitude\n"
"is $t_\\alpha = V / \\Delta_\\alpha$. The [Appendix](#appendix) explains why the first-order amplitude is\n"
"the choice used in this tutorial rather than the exact two-level angle.\n"
msgstr ""
"yang mengestimasi berapa banyak energi korelasi yang dibawa oleh setiap eksitasi. Dua angka yang sama menentukan\n"
"sudut circuit: dengan $V = \\langle \\Phi_{\\mathrm{ref}} | H | \\alpha \\rangle$, amplitudo orde pertama\n"
"adalah $t_\\alpha = V / \\Delta_\\alpha$. [Appendix](#appendix) menjelaskan mengapa amplitudo orde pertama menjadi\n"
"pilihan yang digunakan dalam tutorial ini, bukan sudut dua-level yang eksak.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Qubit-excitation blocks {#qubit-excitation-blocks}"
msgstr "Blok eksitasi-qubit {#qubit-excitation-blocks}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Under the Jordan-Wigner mapping a particle-conserving $2p2h$ excitation operator becomes a sum of\n"
"eight Pauli strings, each carrying a string of $Z$ operators between the outermost indices. The\n"
"$Z$ strings enforce fermionic antisymmetry, and they are expensive: a proton-neutron\n"
"excitation spans the boundary between the two halves of the register and includes a parity string\n"
"across that boundary.\n"
msgstr ""
"Di bawah pemetaan Jordan-Wigner, operator eksitasi $2p2h$ yang mengonservasi particle menjadi jumlah dari\n"
"delapan string Pauli, masing-masing membawa string operator $Z$ di antara indeks terluar. String\n"
"$Z$ ini menegakkan antisimetri fermionic, dan mahal secara komputasi: eksitasi proton-neutron\n"
"membentang melintasi batas antara dua bagian register dan mencakup string parity\n"
"melintasi batas tersebut.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Dropping the $Z$ strings gives the *qubit-excitation* operator of Yordanov et al.\n"
"[\\[5\\]](#references). The state prepared by this operator has different amplitudes, but it connects exactly the same pairs of determinants, so the set of determinants the circuit can\n"
"reach is unchanged. Pooled SQD uses these determinants for the classical diagonalization. Step 2 compares\n"
"the support of the two constructions and measures their hardware costs.\n"
msgstr ""
"Menghilangkan string $Z$ menghasilkan operator *qubit-excitation* dari Yordanov et al.\n"
"[\\[5\\]](#references). State yang disiapkan oleh operator ini memiliki amplitudo yang berbeda, tapi ia menghubungkan pasangan determinant yang persis sama, sehingga himpunan determinant yang bisa dijangkau\n"
"circuit tidak berubah. Pooled SQD menggunakan determinant ini untuk diagonalisasi klasik. Step 2 membandingkan\n"
"support dari kedua konstruksi ini dan mengukur biaya hardware-nya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Building the Pauli form from $a_j^\\dagger = \\tfrac{1}{2}(X_j - i Y_j) \\otimes Z_{<j}$, with the $Z$\n"
"string optional, keeps the two constructions a single flag apart. All eight terms of one generator\n"
"commute, so a single `PauliEvolutionGate` step is the exact exponential rather than a Trotter\n"
"approximation to it.\n"
msgstr ""
"Membangun bentuk Pauli dari $a_j^\\dagger = \\tfrac{1}{2}(X_j - i Y_j) \\otimes Z_{<j}$, dengan string $Z$\n"
"opsional, menjaga kedua konstruksi ini hanya berbeda satu flag. Kedelapan term dari satu generator\n"
"commute, sehingga satu step `PauliEvolutionGate` adalah eksponensial eksak, bukan aproksimasi\n"
"Trotter darinya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The depth budget and the circuit ensemble {#the-depth-budget-and-the-circuit-ensemble}"
msgstr "Budget depth dan ensemble circuit {#the-depth-budget-and-the-circuit-ensemble}"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A single deep circuit containing every ranked excitation can exceed the hardware's coherence time. Spreading the pool\n"
"over an *ensemble* of shallow circuits and pooling their shots into one determinant set turns Step 2\n"
"into a packing problem: each excitation has a measured cost, each circuit has a budget, and the\n"
"question is how much of the ranked pool fits.\n"
msgstr ""
"Satu circuit dalam yang berisi setiap eksitasi yang diranking bisa melebihi coherence time hardware. Menyebarkan pool\n"
"ke sebuah *ensemble* circuit yang dangkal dan menggabungkan shot-nya menjadi satu himpunan determinant mengubah Step 2\n"
"menjadi masalah packing: setiap eksitasi memiliki biaya yang terukur, setiap circuit memiliki budget, dan\n"
"pertanyaannya adalah seberapa banyak pool yang diranking bisa muat.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The budget is measured in **two-qubit depth** (layers of two-qubit gates on the critical path)\n"
"rather than in a raw gate count, because depth sets the circuit's duration and therefore how\n"
"much of the device's coherence it spends. The total count is reported alongside it, since that is the\n"
"better proxy for accumulated gate error; the two answer different questions and neither substitutes\n"
"for the other.\n"
msgstr ""
"Budget diukur dalam **depth dua-qubit** (layer gate dua-qubit pada critical path)\n"
"bukan dalam raw gate count, karena depth menentukan durasi circuit dan karenanya seberapa\n"
"banyak coherence device yang dihabiskan. Total count dilaporkan bersamaan dengannya, karena itu adalah\n"
"proxy yang lebih baik untuk error gate yang terakumulasi; keduanya menjawab pertanyaan yang berbeda dan tidak ada yang bisa\n"
"menggantikan yang lain.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Both quantities are extracted by *arity*: an instruction acting on exactly two qubits, whatever the\n"
"backend happens to call its entangling gate. Matching on gate names instead could return zero\n"
"for an unfamiliar basis set, incorrectly placing the whole pool in one circuit without exceeding\n"
"the computed budget.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kedua kuantitas ini diekstrak berdasarkan *arity*: sebuah instruksi yang bekerja pada tepat dua qubit, apa pun\n"
"nama yang dipakai backend untuk entangling gate-nya. Mencocokkan berdasarkan nama gate malah bisa mengembalikan nol\n"
"untuk basis set yang tidak dikenal, secara keliru menempatkan seluruh pool dalam satu circuit tanpa melebihi\n"
"budget yang dihitung.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Filling whichever circuit is currently emptiest, in rank order, keeps every circuit near the budget.\n"
"Costs are measured on the real backend target, one excitation at a time, because a cost read off an\n"
"abstract circuit is not the cost the transpiler produces.\n"
msgstr ""
"Mengisi circuit mana pun yang saat ini paling kosong, dalam urutan ranking, menjaga setiap circuit tetap mendekati budget.\n"
"Biaya diukur pada target backend nyata, satu eksitasi pada satu waktu, karena biaya yang dibaca dari\n"
"circuit abstrak bukan biaya yang dihasilkan transpiler.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Post-processing: repair, recombine, diagonalize {#post-processing-repair-recombine-diagonalize}"
msgstr "Post-processing: repair, rekombinasi, diagonalisasi {#post-processing-repair-recombine-diagonalize}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Three helpers do the work of Step 4.\n"
msgstr "Tiga helper melakukan pekerjaan Step 4.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`half_configurations` splits each sampled row into a proton half and a neutron half, and keeps each\n"
"half that has the correct nucleon number. A row with a valid proton half contributes that half even if its\n"
"neutron half has the wrong nucleon number. Each half carries the total sampled weight of the rows it appeared in, which\n"
"is what ranks it if the subspace needs to be truncated.\n"
msgstr ""
"`half_configurations` memecah setiap baris yang tersampel menjadi bagian proton dan bagian neutron, dan menyimpan setiap\n"
"bagian yang memiliki jumlah nukleon yang benar. Baris dengan bagian proton yang valid tetap menyumbang bagian itu meskipun\n"
"bagian neutronnya memiliki jumlah nukleon yang salah. Setiap bagian membawa total bobot sampel dari baris tempat ia muncul, yang\n"
"menjadi dasar rankingnya jika subspace perlu dipotong.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`grow_subspace` recombines the halves into every product that lands in the target $M_J$ and parity\n"
"sector, *adding* to the subspace it is given rather than rebuilding it. That keeps successive\n"
"subspaces nested, which is what makes the energy sequence monotone non-increasing instead of merely\n"
"fluctuating around a bound.\n"
msgstr ""
"`grow_subspace` merekombinasi bagian-bagian tersebut menjadi setiap produk yang jatuh pada sektor $M_J$\n"
"dan parity target, *menambahkan* ke subspace yang diberikan alih-alih membangunnya ulang. Itu membuat\n"
"subspace berurutan tetap bersarang, yang membuat urutan energi menjadi monoton non-increasing, bukan sekadar\n"
"berfluktuasi di sekitar suatu batas.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`recovery_loop` is the self-consistent configuration recovery of the pooled SQD paper\n"
"[\\[1\\]](#references): repair the two half-register nucleon numbers against the current occupancy\n"
"estimate, recombine, diagonalize, and take the next occupancy estimate from the eigenvector.\n"
msgstr ""
"`recovery_loop` adalah pemulihan konfigurasi self-consistent dari paper pooled SQD\n"
"[\\[1\\]](#references): perbaiki kedua jumlah nukleon half-register terhadap estimasi occupancy\n"
"saat ini, rekombinasi, diagonalisasi, dan ambil estimasi occupancy berikutnya dari eigenvector.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Check the bit-ordering conventions carefully to avoid incorrect results. `qiskit-addon-sqd` writes column 0 of its\n"
"bitstring matrix as the *highest* qubit index, so reversing a row gives occupation indexed by qubit;\n"
"its \"right\" half is the low qubit indices, which is the proton block. Correspondingly,\n"
"`recover_configurations` takes `num_elec_a` as the proton number and average occupancies ordered\n"
"`(protons, neutrons)` by qubit index. The addon assumes bit $i$ pairs with bit $i + N$; in this\n"
"register, proton qubit $i$ and neutron qubit $i + N$ are the same $(n, \\ell, j, m_j)$ state, so the\n"
"assumption is physically meaningful here rather than incidental.\n"
msgstr ""
"Periksa konvensi bit-ordering dengan cermat untuk menghindari hasil yang salah. `qiskit-addon-sqd` menulis kolom 0 dari\n"
"matriks bitstring-nya sebagai indeks qubit *tertinggi*, sehingga membalik satu baris memberikan occupation yang diindeks berdasarkan qubit;\n"
"bagian \"kanan\"-nya adalah indeks qubit rendah, yang merupakan blok proton. Sejalan dengan itu,\n"
"`recover_configurations` mengambil `num_elec_a` sebagai jumlah proton dan rata-rata occupancy yang diurutkan\n"
"`(protons, neutrons)` berdasarkan indeks qubit. Addon ini mengasumsikan bit $i$ berpasangan dengan bit $i + N$; dalam\n"
"register ini, qubit proton $i$ dan qubit neutron $i + N$ adalah state $(n, \\ell, j, m_j)$ yang sama, sehingga\n"
"asumsi ini bermakna secara fisik di sini, bukan kebetulan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Backend, budget, and run parameters {#backend-budget-and-run-parameters}"
msgstr "Backend, budget, dan parameter run {#backend-budget-and-run-parameters}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Every run that follows uses the same backend, the same pass managers, and the same depth budget, so the three\n"
"are directly comparable. The budget ties them together: every circuit in every\n"
"ensemble has to fit inside it, and it decides how much of a pool can be sampled at all.\n"
msgstr ""
"Setiap run berikutnya menggunakan backend yang sama, pass manager yang sama, dan budget depth yang sama, sehingga ketiganya\n"
"bisa langsung dibandingkan. Budget-lah yang mengikat mereka bersama: setiap circuit dalam setiap\n"
"ensemble harus muat di dalamnya, dan budget itu menentukan seberapa banyak pool yang bisa disampel sama sekali.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The values here were chosen by measuring transpiled cost against a Heron target. At a two-qubit depth of 300 and 16 circuits, both 24-qubit and 40-qubit ensembles come out well under 100 microseconds per\n"
"circuit, against coherence times of a few hundred microseconds. Increasing the budget includes more of the pool but increases circuit duration. Measure this\n"
"tradeoff for your backend.\n"
msgstr ""
"Nilai-nilai di sini dipilih dengan mengukur biaya yang sudah ditranspilasi terhadap target Heron. Pada depth dua-qubit 300 dan 16 circuit, ensemble 24-qubit maupun 40-qubit sama-sama berada jauh di bawah 100 mikrodetik per\n"
"circuit, dibandingkan dengan coherence time sekitar beberapa ratus mikrodetik. Menaikkan budget mencakup lebih banyak pool tapi meningkatkan durasi circuit. Ukur\n"
"tradeoff ini untuk backend Anda.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Small-scale hardware example {#small-scale-hardware-example}"
msgstr "Contoh hardware skala kecil {#small-scale-hardware-example}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This section follows the four-step workflow on a QPU, using the same backend and the same\n"
"gate budget as the large-scale runs. The smaller problem provides an exact reference for checking the result.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bagian ini mengikuti workflow empat-langkah pada QPU, menggunakan backend yang sama dan gate budget yang sama\n"
"dengan run skala besar. Problem yang lebih kecil ini menyediakan referensi eksak untuk memeriksa hasilnya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The small-scale problem is $^{20}\\mathrm{Ne}$: two valence protons and two valence neutrons in the\n"
"$sd$ shell above an $^{16}\\mathrm{O}$ core, with the USDA interaction [\\[2\\]](#references). Three\n"
"orbitals per species give 24 qubits, and the complete symmetry-allowed basis is 640 determinants,\n"
"small enough to compare the energy estimates with the exact answer.\n"
msgstr ""
"Problem skala kecil adalah $^{20}\\mathrm{Ne}$: dua proton valence dan dua neutron valence dalam\n"
"shell $sd$ di atas core $^{16}\\mathrm{O}$, dengan interaksi USDA [\\[2\\]](#references). Tiga\n"
"orbital per spesies memberikan 24 qubit, dan basis lengkap yang diizinkan simetri adalah 640 determinant,\n"
"cukup kecil untuk membandingkan estimasi energi dengan jawaban eksak.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Map classical inputs to a quantum problem {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"
msgstr "Step 1: Memetakan input klasik ke problem kuantum {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Read the interaction, build the register, and construct the reference determinant. The following table shows the register information from the [Background](#background), read directly\n"
"from the interaction file.\n"
msgstr ""
"Baca interaksinya, bangun register, dan konstruksi determinant referensi. Tabel berikut menunjukkan informasi register dari [Background](#background), yang dibaca langsung\n"
"dari file interaksi.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Run two checks on the Hamiltonian before continuing. Both are inexpensive and can reveal\n"
"recoupling errors that a single energy calculation might not detect.\n"
msgstr ""
"Jalankan dua pemeriksaan pada Hamiltonian sebelum melanjutkan. Keduanya murah secara komputasi dan bisa mengungkap\n"
"error recoupling yang mungkin tidak terdeteksi oleh satu perhitungan energi saja.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A rotationally invariant Hamiltonian organizes its eigenstates into $J$ multiplets, so every\n"
"eigenvalue of the $M_J = 2$ sector must also appear in the $M_J = 0$ spectrum at the same energy. The gap between the ground state and the lowest state carrying $M_J = 2$ is the $2^+$ excitation\n"
"energy, which is measured: $1.634$ MeV for $^{20}\\mathrm{Ne}$ [\\[6\\]](#references). An empirical\n"
"$sd$-shell interaction is expected to agree within a few hundred keV.\n"
msgstr ""
"Hamiltonian yang invariant secara rotasi mengorganisasikan eigenstate-nya ke dalam multiplet $J$, sehingga setiap\n"
"eigenvalue dari sektor $M_J = 2$ juga harus muncul dalam spektrum $M_J = 0$ pada energi yang sama. Selisih antara ground state dan state terendah yang membawa $M_J = 2$ adalah energi eksitasi\n"
"$2^+$, yang terukur: $1.634$ MeV untuk $^{20}\\mathrm{Ne}$ [\\[6\\]](#references). Interaksi shell-$sd$\n"
"empiris diharapkan cocok dalam beberapa ratus keV.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next, construct the operator pool. Applying the two selection rules gives an important result: for this reference, in this model space, **there are no allowed single excitations at all**.\n"
msgstr "Selanjutnya, konstruksi pool operator. Menerapkan kedua aturan seleksi memberikan hasil penting: untuk referensi ini, dalam ruang model ini, **tidak ada eksitasi tunggal yang diizinkan sama sekali**.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A $1p1h$ excitation conserves $M_J$ only if the particle state\n"
"has the same $m_j$ as the hole. The reference occupies the two states of largest $|m_j|$ in the\n"
"lowest orbital ($m_j = \\pm 5/2$ of $0d_{5/2}$), and no other orbital in the $sd$ shell reaches\n"
"$|m_j| = 5/2$, since $0d_{3/2}$ stops at $3/2$ and $1s_{1/2}$ at $1/2$. Therefore, no single excitation\n"
"survives, and correlation is carried entirely by $2p2h$ excitations. This is a property of the\n"
"reference and the shell, not a general law; the following cell counts it rather than assuming it.\n"
msgstr "Eksitasi $1p1h$ mengonservasi $M_J$ hanya jika state particle memiliki $m_j$ yang sama dengan hole-nya. Referensi ini menempati dua state dengan $|m_j|$ terbesar di orbital terendah ($m_j = \\pm 5/2$ dari $0d_{5/2}$), dan tidak ada orbital lain dalam shell $sd$ yang mencapai $|m_j| = 5/2$, karena $0d_{3/2}$ berhenti di $3/2$ dan $1s_{1/2}$ di $1/2$. Karena itu, tidak ada eksitasi tunggal yang bertahan, dan korelasi dibawa sepenuhnya oleh eksitasi $2p2h$. Ini adalah properti dari referensi dan shell tersebut, bukan hukum umum; cell berikut menghitungnya, bukan mengasumsikannya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Optimize problem for quantum hardware execution {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"
msgstr "Step 2: Mengoptimalkan problem untuk eksekusi pada hardware kuantum {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Transpilation reveals the hardware cost of the Jordan-Wigner $Z$ strings and the savings from\n"
"using qubit excitations. The first cell measures both constructions against the real backend\n"
"target and checks the claim, introduced in the [Setup](#setup), that dropping the $Z$ strings changes the\n"
"amplitudes but not the set of determinants the circuit can reach.\n"
msgstr ""
"Transpilasi mengungkap biaya hardware dari string $Z$ Jordan-Wigner dan penghematan dari\n"
"penggunaan eksitasi qubit. Cell pertama mengukur kedua konstruksi terhadap target backend\n"
"nyata dan memeriksa klaim, yang diperkenalkan di [Setup](#setup), bahwa menghilangkan string $Z$ mengubah\n"
"amplitudo tapi tidak mengubah himpunan determinant yang bisa dijangkau circuit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Compare two consequences of this substitution. A qubit excitation costs the same regardless of the distance between its\n"
"indices, so proton-neutron excitations, which span the boundary between the two halves of the\n"
"register and make up most of the pool, no longer have this additional cost. The whole pool then\n"
"fits inside the budget, which means the limit on the result is sampling rather than circuit depth.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bandingkan dua konsekuensi dari substitusi ini. Eksitasi qubit memiliki biaya yang sama tidak peduli jarak antara\n"
"indeksnya, sehingga eksitasi proton-neutron, yang membentang melintasi batas antara dua bagian\n"
"register dan menyusun sebagian besar pool, tidak lagi memiliki biaya tambahan ini. Seluruh pool kemudian\n"
"muat di dalam budget, yang berarti batasan pada hasilnya adalah sampling, bukan depth circuit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3: Execute using Qiskit primitives {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-primitives}"
msgstr "Step 3: Mengeksekusi menggunakan Qiskit primitives {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-primitives}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Submit one job per problem, with the whole ensemble as a single list of circuits. Gate and\n"
"measurement twirling and dynamical decoupling are enabled to reduce the effects of hardware noise.\n"
"Their benefit depends on the circuit and backend.\n"
msgstr ""
"Submit satu job per problem, dengan seluruh ensemble sebagai satu list circuit tunggal. Gate dan\n"
"measurement twirling serta dynamical decoupling diaktifkan untuk mengurangi efek noise hardware.\n"
"Manfaatnya bergantung pada circuit dan backend.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Each job's ID is printed. Use `service.job(\"JOB_ID\")` to retrieve the completed job and its\n"
"results without using additional QPU time.\n"
msgstr ""
"ID masing-masing job dicetak. Gunakan `service.job(\"JOB_ID\")` untuk mengambil job yang sudah selesai beserta\n"
"hasilnya tanpa menggunakan waktu QPU tambahan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 4: Post-process and return result in desired classical format {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"
msgstr "Langkah 4: Post-proses dan kembalikan hasil dalam format klasik yang diinginkan {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Convert the quantum samples into an energy estimate using the nuclear-symmetry constraints\n"
"described in the [Background](#background) section.\n"
msgstr ""
"Konversikan sampel kuantum menjadi estimasi energi menggunakan batasan simetri nuklir\n"
"yang dijelaskan pada bagian [Latar Belakang](#background).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Configuration recovery repairs the two nucleon numbers.** `recover_configurations` takes each shot that\n"
"has the wrong number of protons or neutrons and flips the bits least consistent with the current\n"
"estimate of the average orbital occupancies, instead of discarding it. On the first pass the\n"
"occupancy estimate comes from the shots that already survived; afterward it comes from the\n"
"eigenvector of the previous subspace, which makes the procedure self-consistent.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Pemulihan konfigurasi memperbaiki dua bilangan nukleon.** `recover_configurations` mengambil setiap shot yang\n"
"memiliki jumlah proton atau neutron yang salah dan membalik bit yang paling tidak konsisten dengan\n"
"estimasi okupansi orbital rata-rata saat ini, alih-alih membuangnya. Pada pass pertama\n"
"estimasi okupansi berasal dari shot yang sudah bertahan; setelah itu berasal dari\n"
"eigenvector subspace sebelumnya, yang membuat prosedur ini self-consistent.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**$M_J$ and parity are imposed on the recombined products, not on whole shots.** Every repaired shot\n"
"contributes a proton half and a neutron half, and the subspace is spanned by every product of a\n"
"sampled proton configuration with a sampled neutron configuration that lands at $M_J = 0$ with the\n"
"right parity. Filtering whole shots on total $M_J$ instead would throw away two good halves for the\n"
"sake of a quantum number that belongs to their combination.\n"
msgstr ""
"**$M_J$ dan paritas diberlakukan pada produk yang digabungkan kembali, bukan pada seluruh shot.** Setiap\n"
"shot yang diperbaiki menyumbangkan setengah bagian proton dan setengah bagian neutron, dan subspace\n"
"direntang oleh setiap produk dari konfigurasi proton yang di-sampling dengan konfigurasi neutron yang\n"
"di-sampling yang mendarat pada $M_J = 0$ dengan paritas yang benar. Menyaring seluruh shot berdasarkan\n"
"total $M_J$ malah akan membuang dua bagian yang bagus demi bilangan kuantum yang sebenarnya milik\n"
"kombinasi keduanya.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-09-30
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The four quantum-number checks reject different fractions of samples. The two nucleon numbers\n"
"account for most of the filtering. Parity is *automatically* satisfied inside a single major shell: every $sd$ orbital\n"
"has even $\\ell$ and every $pf$ orbital odd $\\ell$, so once the nucleon numbers are right the parity\n"
"cannot be wrong. The parity check is retained because a cross-shell model space would make it an\n"
"independent constraint. The $M_J$ check keeps products in the target angular-momentum sector. The value of\n"
"having four exact quantum numbers is that they are *cheap and exact*, not that each one is a large\n"
"filter.\n"
msgstr ""
"Empat pemeriksaan bilangan kuantum menolak fraksi sampel yang berbeda-beda. Dua bilangan nukleon\n"
"menyumbang sebagian besar penyaringan. Parity *otomatis* terpenuhi di dalam satu major shell: setiap\n"
"orbital $sd$ memiliki $\\ell$ genap dan setiap orbital $pf$ memiliki $\\ell$ ganjil, jadi begitu bilangan\n"
"nukleon sudah benar, parity tidak mungkin salah. Pemeriksaan parity tetap dipertahankan karena\n"
"model space lintas-shell akan menjadikannya batasan independen. Pemeriksaan $M_J$ menjaga produk tetap\n"
"berada di sektor momentum sudut target. Keunggulan empat bilangan kuantum eksak ini adalah bahwa\n"
"semuanya *murah dan eksak*, bukan karena masing-masing merupakan penyaring besar.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-09-29 · verified 2026-09-30
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Diagonalizing gives a variational upper bound.** Because each iteration's subspace contains the\n"
"last, the sequence of energies falls monotonically, and every entry in it is a rigorous upper bound on\n"
"the true ground-state energy, regardless of the noise in the samples that produced it.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Diagonalisasi memberikan batas atas variasional.** Karena subspace setiap iterasi memuat subspace\n"
"sebelumnya, urutan energi turun secara monoton, dan setiap entri di dalamnya adalah batas atas yang\n"
"rigoris untuk energi ground-state sebenarnya, terlepas dari noise pada sampel yang menghasilkannya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Evaluate the results {#evaluate-the-results}"
msgstr "Evaluasi hasil {#evaluate-the-results}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use the following checks to evaluate your results on a Heron-class backend with these settings:\n"
msgstr "Gunakan pemeriksaan berikut untuk mengevaluasi hasil Anda pada backend kelas Heron dengan pengaturan ini:\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-09-29 · verified 2026-09-30
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Shot survival** on the two nucleon numbers measures the fraction of shots with the correct proton and neutron counts. It can fall as\n"
"the register grows. A survival rate near zero can indicate a problem with circuit execution. Check the ISA depth in Step 2 and the backend's calibration, not the post-processing.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Shot survival** pada dua bilangan nukleon mengukur fraksi shot dengan jumlah proton dan neutron yang benar. Nilai ini dapat menurun\n"
"seiring bertambahnya ukuran register. Tingkat survival mendekati nol dapat menandakan masalah pada eksekusi circuit. Periksa depth ISA di Step 2 dan kalibrasi backend, bukan post-processing-nya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**The recovery loop** should print a subspace dimension that stays constant or grows and an energy that stays constant or falls with\n"
"each iteration. If iteration 1 already reaches `MAX_DIMENSION`, the classical solver rather than the\n"
"sampling is the binding constraint.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Loop pemulihan** seharusnya mencetak dimensi subspace yang tetap konstan atau bertambah, dan energi yang tetap konstan atau menurun\n"
"di setiap iterasi. Jika iterasi 1 sudah mencapai `MAX_DIMENSION`, solver klasik-lah, bukan\n"
"sampling, yang menjadi batasan pengikat.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**The recovered fraction** for $^{20}\\mathrm{Ne}$ should be high, because the ansatz ceiling\n"
"computed in Step 1 is the full 640-determinant space; this run is where sampling, not\n"
"expressiveness, is the only obstacle.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Fraksi yang dipulihkan** untuk $^{20}\\mathrm{Ne}$ seharusnya tinggi, karena ansatz ceiling\n"
"yang dihitung di Langkah 1 adalah ruang 640-determinan penuh; run ini adalah tempat sampling, bukan\n"
"ekspresivitas, menjadi satu-satunya hambatan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**The two assertions** in the preceding cell check the variational bounds. A bound that rises means the\n"
"subspaces stopped being nested, and a bound below the exact energy means something is wrong with the\n"
"Hamiltonian, not with the hardware.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Kedua assertion** pada sel sebelumnya memeriksa batas variasional. Batas yang naik berarti\n"
"subspace berhenti bersifat nested, dan batas di bawah energi eksak berarti ada yang salah dengan\n"
"Hamiltonian, bukan dengan hardware-nya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Counterintuitively, a *noisier* backend can give a slightly better bound than a clean one, because\n"
"errors produce valid half-configurations the ideal circuit would never have sampled, and widening\n"
"a variational subspace cannot raise its lowest eigenvalue. Noisy simulation can demonstrate the same effect; this tutorial shows it with\n"
"hardware samples.\n"
msgstr ""
"Secara counterintuitive, backend yang *lebih noisy* dapat memberikan batas yang sedikit lebih baik daripada backend yang bersih, karena\n"
"error menghasilkan setengah-konfigurasi valid yang tidak akan pernah di-sampling oleh circuit ideal, dan memperlebar\n"
"subspace variasional tidak dapat menaikkan eigenvalue terendahnya. Simulasi noisy dapat mendemonstrasikan efek yang sama; tutorial ini menunjukkannya dengan\n"
"sampel hardware.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
