#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Summary {#summary}"
msgstr "Ringkasan {#summary}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"One workflow, unchanged apart from its inputs, ran on a QPU at three problem sizes: a 24-qubit\n"
"problem you can check exactly, a 40-qubit problem you can still check exactly, and a 40-qubit problem\n"
"with nearly two million basis states beyond this tutorial's exact-diagonalization capacity.\n"
msgstr ""
"Satu workflow, tidak berubah kecuali inputnya, dijalankan pada QPU dengan tiga ukuran masalah: masalah 24-qubit\n"
"yang dapat Anda periksa secara eksak, masalah 40-qubit yang masih dapat Anda periksa secara eksak, dan masalah 40-qubit\n"
"dengan hampir dua juta basis state yang melampaui kapasitas diagonalisasi-eksak tutorial ini.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The three runs illustrate the following points:\n"
msgstr "Ketiga run tersebut menggambarkan poin-poin berikut:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**The quantum step only has to propose determinants.** The circuit is fixed, seeded from\n"
"second-order perturbation theory, and never optimized. Nothing in the workflow needs its amplitudes\n"
"to be accurate, only its support to be useful. Classical diagonalization in the selected subspace gives a\n"
"variational upper bound, although the bound varies with the sampled configurations.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Langkah kuantum hanya perlu mengusulkan determinan.** Circuit-nya tetap, di-seed dari\n"
"teori perturbasi orde-dua, dan tidak pernah dioptimalkan. Tidak ada bagian workflow yang memerlukan amplitudonya\n"
"akurat, hanya support-nya yang perlu berguna. Diagonalisasi klasik dalam subspace yang dipilih memberikan\n"
"batas atas variasional, meskipun batas tersebut bervariasi dengan konfigurasi yang di-sampling.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Qubit excitations reduce circuit depth.** Because only the support matters, the fermionic excitation blocks\n"
"can be replaced by qubit excitations, whose cost does not grow with the distance between the\n"
"orbitals they connect. Step 2 measured the saving on the actual backend, which is the difference\n"
"between a circuit that fits comfortably inside coherence and one that does not.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Eksitasi qubit mengurangi kedalaman circuit.** Karena hanya support yang penting, blok eksitasi fermionik\n"
"dapat digantikan oleh eksitasi qubit, yang biayanya tidak bertambah seiring jarak antar\n"
"orbital yang dihubungkannya. Langkah 2 mengukur penghematan tersebut pada backend sesungguhnya, yaitu selisih\n"
"antara circuit yang muat dengan nyaman di dalam coherence dan yang tidak.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Configuration recovery reuses noisy samples.** Every shot with the wrong proton or neutron number is repaired\n"
"against the current occupancy estimate rather than discarded, and each repaired half-configuration\n"
"can add configurations to the subspace. Widening a variational subspace cannot raise its lowest\n"
"eigenvalue. This tutorial demonstrates configuration recovery using hardware samples.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Pemulihan konfigurasi menggunakan kembali sampel yang noisy.** Setiap shot dengan jumlah proton atau neutron yang salah diperbaiki\n"
"berdasarkan estimasi okupansi saat ini alih-alih dibuang, dan setiap setengah-konfigurasi yang diperbaiki\n"
"dapat menambahkan konfigurasi ke subspace. Memperlebar subspace variasional tidak dapat menaikkan\n"
"eigenvalue terendahnya. Tutorial ini mendemonstrasikan pemulihan konfigurasi menggunakan sampel hardware.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**The binding constraint moves as you scale.** At 24 qubits the ansatz could reach the exact answer,\n"
"and only sampling stood in the way. At 40 qubits with four valence nucleons per species, the gate\n"
"budget covers a minority of the pool and the dense classical solver caps the subspace. Knowing which\n"
"of the three is limiting you is the practical skill this workflow teaches.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Batasan pengikat berpindah seiring skala.** Pada 24 qubit, ansatz dapat mencapai jawaban eksak,\n"
"dan hanya sampling yang menjadi penghalang. Pada 40 qubit dengan empat nukleon valensi per spesies, gate\n"
"budget hanya mencakup sebagian kecil pool dan solver klasik dense membatasi subspace. Mengetahui mana\n"
"dari ketiganya yang membatasi Anda adalah keterampilan praktis yang diajarkan workflow ini.\n"

