# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Background (Fortran) {#background-fortran}"
msgstr "Latar belakang (Fortran) {#background-fortran}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The nuclear shell model treats a nucleus as a few *valence* nucleons moving in a small set of single-particle orbitals above an inert *core*, interacting through an empirical two-body force fitted to measured spectra. Its computational cost is combinatorial: the basis is every way of distributing the valence protons and neutrons over the available states, and this growth limits the model spaces accessible to exact diagonalization.\n"
msgstr "Model shell nuklir memperlakukan nukleus sebagai beberapa nukleon *valence* yang bergerak dalam sekumpulan kecil orbital single-particle di atas *core* yang inert, berinteraksi melalui gaya dua-body empiris yang dicocokkan dengan spektrum yang terukur. Biaya komputasinya bersifat kombinatorial: basisnya adalah setiap cara mendistribusikan proton dan neutron valence pada state yang tersedia, dan pertumbuhan ini membatasi ruang model yang bisa diakses oleh diagonalisasi eksak.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pooled sample-based quantum diagonalization (pooled SQD) [\\[1\\]](#references) splits that problem in two. A quantum circuit is used only to *propose* which basis states matter. It is measured in the computational basis, and each measured bitstring names one Slater determinant. The Hamiltonian is then built and diagonalized classically in the span of those determinants. Because the classical step is an exact diagonalization inside a subspace, it returns a variational upper bound on the true ground-state energy.\n"
msgstr "Diagonalisasi kuantum berbasis sampel gabungan (pooled SQD) [\\[1\\]](#references) membagi problem tersebut menjadi dua. Circuit kuantum hanya digunakan untuk *mengusulkan* basis state mana yang penting. Ia diukur dalam basis komputasional, dan setiap bitstring yang terukur menamai satu determinant Slater. Hamiltonian kemudian dibangun dan didiagonalisasi secara klasik dalam span determinant-determinant tersebut. Karena langkah klasik ini adalah diagonalisasi eksak di dalam sebuah subspace, ia mengembalikan batas atas variational pada energi ground-state yang sebenarnya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Noise changes *which* determinants the circuit proposes, but it does not enter the classical Hamiltonian. A shot that violates a conserved quantity is discarded, and a shot that survives is a legitimate basis vector however it was produced. Noise therefore costs subspace quality, not correctness. Nuclear structure provides several exact quantum numbers for this check: a physical determinant must carry the right number of valence protons *and* valence neutrons, the right total angular-momentum projection $M_J$, and the right parity.\n"
msgstr "Noise mengubah determinan *mana* yang diusulkan Circuit, tetapi tidak masuk ke Hamiltonian klasik. Shot yang melanggar besaran yang kekal dibuang, dan shot yang bertahan adalah vektor basis yang sah bagaimanapun cara menghasilkannya. Jadi noise mengorbankan kualitas subruang, bukan kebenaran. Struktur nuklir menyediakan beberapa bilangan kuantum eksak untuk pemeriksaan ini: determinan fisik harus memiliki jumlah proton valensi *dan* neutron valensi yang tepat, proyeksi momentum sudut total $M_J$ yang tepat, dan paritas yang tepat.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Fortran application uses the same register as the Python example. Every qubit is one $m$-scheme single-particle state $(n, \\ell, j, m_j, t_z)$, and $|1\\rangle$ means occupied. Protons come first, then neutrons; within a species, orbitals follow the order of the interaction file; within an orbital, $m_j$ descends. The $^{20}\\mathrm{Ne}$ example here uses this 24-qubit $sd$-shell register.\n"
msgstr "Aplikasi Fortran memakai register yang sama dengan contoh Python. Setiap qubit adalah satu state partikel-tunggal skema-$m$ $(n, \\ell, j, m_j, t_z)$, dan $|1\\rangle$ berarti terisi. Proton datang lebih dulu, lalu neutron; dalam satu spesies, orbital mengikuti urutan file interaksi; dalam satu orbital, $m_j$ menurun. Contoh $^{20}\\mathrm{Ne}$ di sini memakai register shell-$sd$ 24-qubit ini.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Hamiltonian is a one-body term plus a two-body interaction,\n"
msgstr "Hamiltonian adalah term one-body ditambah interaksi two-body,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"H = \\sum_{p} \\varepsilon_p\\, a_p^\\dagger a_p\n"
"  + \\tfrac{1}{4}\\sum_{pqrs} \\langle pq \\| rs \\rangle\\, a_p^\\dagger a_q^\\dagger a_s a_r ,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"H = \\sum_{p} \\varepsilon_p\\, a_p^\\dagger a_p\n"
"  + \\tfrac{1}{4}\\sum_{pqrs} \\langle pq \\| rs \\rangle\\, a_p^\\dagger a_q^\\dagger a_s a_r ,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where $p,q,r,s$ label $m$-scheme states. The interaction file tabulates two-body matrix elements in the $J$-coupled basis of orbitals, and the application recovers each $m$-scheme element $\\langle pq \\| rs \\rangle$ by Clebsch-Gordan recoupling. The regression test in [Check the workflow locally](#check-the-workflow-locally) confirms that this produces the same Hamiltonian as the Python example.\n"
msgstr "di mana $p,q,r,s$ melabeli state skema-$m$. File interaksi mentabulasi elemen matriks dua-benda dalam basis orbital terkopel-$J$, dan aplikasi memulihkan setiap elemen skema-$m$ $\\langle pq \\| rs \\rangle$ lewat rekopling Clebsch-Gordan. Uji regresi di [Periksa workflow secara lokal](#check-the-workflow-locally) mengonfirmasi bahwa ini menghasilkan Hamiltonian yang sama dengan contoh Python.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Fortran workflow {#the-fortran-workflow}"
msgstr "Workflow Fortran {#the-fortran-workflow}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Reference determinant.** Fill the lowest single-particle-energy $(+m_j, -m_j)$ pairs of each species, which gives $M_J = 0$.\n"
msgstr "**Determinan referensi.** Isi pasangan $(+m_j, -m_j)$ berenergi partikel-tunggal terendah untuk setiap spesies, yang menghasilkan $M_J = 0$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Excitation pool.** Generate the single and double excitations of the reference allowed by angular-momentum coupling, rank them by a second-order perturbation-theory score, $V^2/|\\Delta|$, and seed each with its two-level mixing angle.\n"
msgstr "**Pool eksitasi.** Hasilkan eksitasi tunggal dan ganda dari referensi yang diizinkan oleh kopling momentum sudut, urutkan berdasarkan skor teori perturbasi orde kedua, $V^2/|\\Delta|$, dan inisialisasi masing-masing dengan sudut pencampuran dua-levelnya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Circuit ensemble.** Each circuit prepares the reference and applies the next slice of the ranked pool: Givens rotations for single excitations and qubit-excitation gates for double excitations. With the default of 16 excitations per circuit, 11 circuits cover the whole double-excitation pool for $^{20}\\mathrm{Ne}$.\n"
msgstr "**Ensemble Circuit.** Setiap Circuit menyiapkan referensi dan menerapkan irisan berikutnya dari pool yang telah diurutkan: rotasi Givens untuk eksitasi tunggal dan gate qubit-excitation untuk eksitasi ganda. Dengan default 16 eksitasi per Circuit, 11 Circuit mencakup seluruh pool eksitasi ganda untuk $^{20}\\mathrm{Ne}$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Sample.** Transpile each circuit and sample it on a QPU.\n"
msgstr "**Sampling.** Transpile setiap Circuit dan lakukan sampling di QPU.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '5. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Filter.** Keep only shots with the right proton number, neutron number, $M_J$, and parity, and discard the rest.\n"
msgstr "**Penyaringan.** Simpan hanya shot dengan jumlah proton, jumlah neutron, $M_J$, dan paritas yang tepat, dan buang sisanya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '6. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Diagonalize.** Build the Hamiltonian in the span of the unique kept determinants, pooled across all circuits, and diagonalize it with LAPACK to get a variational upper bound. Alternatively, diagonalize each circuit's samples separately.\n"
msgstr "**Diagonalisasi.** Bangun Hamiltonian dalam rentang determinan unik yang dipertahankan, dipool dari semua Circuit, dan diagonalisasi dengan LAPACK untuk mendapatkan batas atas variasional. Alternatifnya, diagonalisasi sampel setiap Circuit secara terpisah.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each step maps to a source file in the Fortran directory:\n"
msgstr "Setiap langkah dipetakan ke satu file source di direktori Fortran:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Step | Source |\n"
"|---|---|\n"
"| Read the interaction and recouple to the $m$-scheme | `physics/usdb_reader.f90`, `physics/clebsch_gordan.f90`, `physics/orbital_registry.f90` |\n"
"| Rank and seed the excitation pool | `nuclear_pool.f90`, `nuclear_selection.f90` |\n"
"| Build the circuits | `circuit/nuclear_ansatz.f90`, `nuclear_gates.f90` |\n"
"| Sample, filter, and diagonalize | `circuit/nuclear_shell_driver.f90`, `physics/symmetry_filter.f90`, `physics/exact_solver.f90` |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Langkah | Sumber |\n"
"|---|---|\n"
"| Membaca interaksi dan mengkopling ulang ke skema-$m$ | `physics/usdb_reader.f90`, `physics/clebsch_gordan.f90`, `physics/orbital_registry.f90` |\n"
"| Meranking dan menyemai pool eksitasi | `nuclear_pool.f90`, `nuclear_selection.f90` |\n"
"| Membangun circuit | `circuit/nuclear_ansatz.f90`, `nuclear_gates.f90` |\n"
"| Sampling, memfilter, dan mendiagonalisasi | `circuit/nuclear_shell_driver.f90`, `physics/symmetry_filter.f90`, `physics/exact_solver.f90` |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Fortran workflow differs from the Python example in several choices, such as how it picks the reference determinant and how it handles samples with the wrong symmetry. [Differences from the Python example](#differences-from-the-python-example) lists them.\n"
msgstr "Workflow Fortran berbeda dari contoh Python dalam beberapa pilihan, misalnya cara memilih determinan referensi dan cara menangani sampel dengan simetri yang salah. [Perbedaan dari contoh Python](#differences-from-the-python-example) merincinya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Requirements (Fortran) {#requirements-fortran}"
msgstr "Persyaratan (Fortran) {#requirements-fortran}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This implementation is adapted from the nuclear shell-model application in [qiskit-fortran](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit-fortran), the Fortran bindings for Qiskit. Build and run the version in the Fortran directory linked in the preceding note rather than the upstream application, because it includes corrections to interaction mass scaling and antisymmetrized pair-exchange phases.\n"
msgstr "Implementasi ini diadaptasi dari aplikasi shell-model nuklir di [qiskit-fortran](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit-fortran), binding Fortran untuk Qiskit. Build dan jalankan versi di direktori Fortran yang ditautkan pada catatan sebelumnya, bukan aplikasi upstream-nya, karena versi itu memuat koreksi untuk penskalaan massa interaksi dan fase pertukaran pasangan yang diantisimetrisasi.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Follow the [build instructions](https://github.com/Qiskit/documentation/blob/main/docs/tutorials/assets/nuclear_sqd_pooled/fortran/BUILD_INSTRUCTIONS.md) to build the Qiskit C library, the Fortran bindings, and this application. The build instructions set `NUCLEAR_SRC` to the Fortran directory and `NUCLEAR_DEPS` to a separate directory for the dependencies; the commands in this example use those variables. Use the same Fortran compiler for the bindings and the application, because module files are compiler-specific. Building the Qiskit C library (`make c`) takes several minutes.\n"
msgstr "Ikuti [petunjuk build](https://github.com/Qiskit/documentation/blob/main/docs/tutorials/assets/nuclear_sqd_pooled/fortran/BUILD_INSTRUCTIONS.md) untuk membangun library C Qiskit, binding Fortran, dan aplikasi ini. Petunjuk build menetapkan `NUCLEAR_SRC` ke direktori Fortran dan `NUCLEAR_DEPS` ke direktori terpisah untuk dependensi; perintah-perintah dalam contoh ini memakai variabel tersebut. Pakai compiler Fortran yang sama untuk binding dan aplikasi, karena file modul bersifat spesifik per compiler. Membangun library C Qiskit (`make c`) memakan waktu beberapa menit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Quantum Compute Client support described in the build instructions is optional. You need it only to submit hardware jobs; the local checks and saved-bitstring processing work without it.\n"
msgstr "Dukungan Quantum Compute Client yang dijelaskan di petunjuk build bersifat opsional. Kamu hanya membutuhkannya untuk mengirim job hardware; pengecekan lokal dan pemrosesan bitstring yang tersimpan tetap jalan tanpa itu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The build produces `nuclear_shell_driver` in `$NUCLEAR_SRC/build` and copies `data/USDB.snt` beside it. Despite its filename, that file contains the **USDA** interaction, as its header states. The supplied example describes two valence protons and two valence neutrons in the $sd$ shell, which is $^{20}\\mathrm{Ne}$, the same nucleus as the Python small-scale hardware example.\n"
msgstr "Build ini menghasilkan `nuclear_shell_driver` di `$NUCLEAR_SRC/build` dan menyalin `data/USDB.snt` ke sebelahnya. Meskipun namanya begitu, file tersebut berisi interaksi **USDA**, seperti yang dinyatakan di headernya. Contoh yang disediakan menggambarkan dua proton valensi dan dua neutron valensi di kulit $sd$, yaitu $^{20}\\mathrm{Ne}$, nukleus yang sama dengan contoh hardware skala kecil di Python.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check the workflow locally {#check-the-workflow-locally}"
msgstr "Cek workflow secara lokal {#check-the-workflow-locally}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "First, run the Hamiltonian regression test:\n"
msgstr "Pertama, jalankan tes regresi Hamiltonian:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The test builds the complete 640-determinant basis for $^{20}\\mathrm{Ne}$, diagonalizes it, and checks that the ground-state energy is $-40.472331$ MeV, the exact energy in the Python example. Passing confirms that the Fortran application builds the same Hamiltonian as the Python example. Because SQD diagonalizes in a subspace of this basis, no run of this application can report an energy below $-40.472331$ MeV for $^{20}\\mathrm{Ne}$; the closer a run gets, the better its sampled subspace.\n"
msgstr "Tes ini membangun basis lengkap 640 determinan untuk $^{20}\\mathrm{Ne}$, mendiagonalisasinya, dan memeriksa bahwa energi ground state adalah $-40.472331$ MeV, energi eksak pada contoh Python. Lolos berarti aplikasi Fortran membangun Hamiltonian yang sama dengan contoh Python. Karena SQD mendiagonalisasi di subruang dari basis ini, tidak ada eksekusi aplikasi ini yang bisa melaporkan energi di bawah $-40.472331$ MeV untuk $^{20}\\mathrm{Ne}$; makin dekat hasilnya, makin bagus subruang yang disampel.\n"

